6c905eaccf6954c86e7ffeefadfe7f54fe1397c966ff2e9e4","event_uuid":"8c36e5fa-acb5-4aa3-98b3-b410b98dd4e3","position":{"commit_sha":"dd380d33f84113f48db396e5a927b35315a9c53d","position":"1787368868906685001-8c36e5fa-acb5-4aa3-98b3-b410b98dd4e3"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null},{"content_hash":"802135bbc2d03634d64d5bf3056695ff3660a085724e8276295727766bdc8783","event_uuid":"7cb1347e-312f-400b-a5a5-35d753a52fc4","position":{"commit_sha":"5e9eedb949fabcefd080065e3a2d0a19564b5500","position":"1787368886824908001-7cb1347e-312f-400b-a5a5-35d753a52fc4"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":null}],"bridge_alerts":[],"bridge_project":null,"claim_harness":"claude-code_2-1-239_agent","claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":"e50ec61e-3a77-4eb8-b56b-c1d0f90ff9bc","comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"Landed in two Gerrit changes, both LLM-Review +1 and Verified +1 then submitted: 2046 (55e308eaaf) collapsed the five tracker-sibling .rebar derivations plus push_state._git_dir into one frozen StorePaths owner, net -96 non-test lines; 2048 (597010b9f1) proved the uniqueness guard FLAGS rather than merely passing, by extracting paths._offending_line and unit-testing it on synthetic lines (including the negative control that ~36 repo_root-derived .rebar joins stay unflagged). AC evidence on landed main: AC1 grep -rn 'def _rebar_dir' src/rebar returns only _store/paths.py:67; AC2 the join-scan branch is covered by four direct classifier tests; AC3 the symlink invariance test passes; AC4 all pinning suites (123 tests) pass with exactly one sanctioned assertion edit (the test_enrich_queue lockstep pin, subsumed by the consolidation); AC5 git diff 55e308eaaf~1..main touches neither gitutil.py nor lock.py. Held-out TDD: 14 tests authored, implementer saw only 2; RED baseline 10 RED / 4 pinning-green; three mutations killed (realpath dropped, sixth copy re-introduced, reason-less escape marker).","timestamp":1787367635407133001}],"completion_expectation":"required","created_at":1787352077784852001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"77f17505-20b0-4585-9cf0-86f04d323179","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"681f-747d-eddc-48ae"},{"link_uuid":"d4d0dae2-0508-45d0-8441-fe215d3bd874","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6dd1-c469-5508-4fea"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\nFive modules derive \"where is `.rebar` / the sidecar directory for this store\" independently: `src/rebar/_store/hlc.py:80` (resolves symlinks), `src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py:65` (resolves after bug `intangible-ladyish-vicuna`), `src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py:57` (resolves after `13f78e3165`), `src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py:104`, `src/rebar/llm/overlap/queue.py:257`; `src/rebar/_store/push_state.py:89-116` parses `.git` by hand for the git dir and `src/rebar/_store/sync.py:281-301` re-derives the git common dir for quarantine. Three of these had the unresolved-symlink bug in turn (`nuclear-calm-heron`, `intangible-ladyish-vicuna`, `conscious-weighable-spittlebug`), each fixed one site per ticket.\n\n## Approach\nAdd `src/rebar/_store/paths.py` with one frozen `StorePaths(tracker)` exposing `canonical` (realpath), `git_dir`, `git_common_dir`, `rebar_dir`, `sidecar(name)`, `log(name)`; every derivation above becomes a call. The class is the only place `os.path.realpath` is applied to a tracker path for sidecar purposes, so an unresolved derivation cannot be re-copied. A guard test asserts no module outside `paths.py` computes `dirname(tracker)`/`.rebar` joins for sidecars (token scan on `\"/.rebar\"` joins plus `_rebar_dir` definitions, owner excluded, `# store-path-ok:` marker escape).\n\n\n## Guard construction\nFollow the guard-test construction rule in the parent epic `airborne-wellloved-kingfisher`: owner module exempt, match the constituent conjunction or AST shape named in Approach (or the definition count where no distinctive atom exists), `# <construct>-ok: <reason>` escape marker, and behaviour pinned only by the named existing tests.\n\n## Scope\n`src/rebar/_store/paths.py` (new), `src/rebar/_store/hlc.py`, `src/rebar/_store/push_state.py`, `src/rebar/_store/sync.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py`, `src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py`, `src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py`, `src/rebar/llm/overlap/queue.py`, `tests/unit/store/test_store_paths.py` (new).\n\n## Testing\nHappy path: a symlinked worktree tracker resolves every sidecar under the canonical store (real `tmp_path` symlink). Edge: a tracker whose `.git` is a gitfile (worktree) yields the common dir. Pinning: `tests/unit/test_compact_trigger.py`, `tests/unit/test_enrich_drain.py`, `tests/unit/test_hlc.py`, `tests/unit/test_push_pending_marker.py`, `tests/scripts/graph/test_doctor_locks.py` pass unchanged.\n\n## Parallel git-dir derivations: enumerated and scoped (review remediation, G1G2)\n`push_state._git_dir` is NOT the only `.git`-gitfile parser. Two more exist and are\n**explicitly OUT of scope for this leaf**:\n- `src/rebar/_store/gitutil.py:70` `_resolve_tracker_git_dir` — same isfile/`gitdir:`/isdir\n  parse, but returns `\"\"` on failure. Consumers: `fsck_scan.py:146`, `fsck_repair.py:415`,\n  `fsck_recover.py:193`, `bridge_repair.py:51`, `tracker_maintenance.py:101`,\n  `gitutil.py:276,357`.\n- `src/rebar/_store/lock.py:156` `_gitdir` — same parse, returns `None` on failure.\n\nRationale for deferring: the three implementations carry **three different failure sentinels**\n(`<tracker>/.git`, `\"\"`, `None`), so unifying them is a behaviour-changing decision about\nwhich sentinel wins at ~9 call sites across the fsck/repair surface — not the mechanical\ncollapse this leaf performs, and outside this leaf's recorded file impact. Two of those call\nsites are monkeypatch seams (`tests/scripts/graph/test_repair_pause_ownership.py:77`,\n`tests/interfaces/store/test_repair_pause_ownership_heldout.py:86`). Tracked as follow-up work\nunder the parent epic rather than smuggled in here.\n\n## Convergence status (review remediation, G7 — parent epic's convergence clause)\nNo latent divergence is converged by this leaf; every collapsed site already resolves symlinks\n**at its composite**, verified by reading each call site:\n- `hlc.py:83` — resolves (`Path(tracker).resolve().parent`).\n- `compact_trigger.py:78` — resolves (via `_canonical_tracker`).\n- `enrich_drain.py:70` — resolves (via `_canonical_tracker`).\n- `queue.py:270` — **resolves**, via a function-local import of\n  `enrich_drain._canonical_tracker`.\n- `doctor_locks.py:115` — the helper itself does a bare `dirname`, but its **only** caller\n  (`doctor_locks.py:335`) passes an already-canonical tracker computed one line earlier at\n  `:334` (`canonical = _lock.canonical_tracker(tracker)`). The composite therefore already\n  resolves, so routing it through `StorePaths` preserves behaviour rather than converging a\n  divergence.\n\nBecause no site changes behaviour, the clause's \"add a test pinning that site's new\ncanonical-resolution\" obligation is discharged by pinning that the behaviour is UNCHANGED: the\nend-to-end test drives all five real sites on a symlinked worktree and asserts every artifact\nalready lands in the one canonical `.rebar`.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [x] `grep -rn \"def _rebar_dir\" src/rebar` returns only `src/rebar/_store/paths.py`; checked by the guard test and the grep.\n- [x] The guard's **join-scan** branch is proven, not just its definition-count branch: a line joining `\".rebar\"` to a `dirname(`/`.parent` step anywhere under `src/rebar` outside the owner is flagged, and a `# store-path-ok: <reason>` marker suppresses it while a reason-less marker does not; checked by the guard's own unit tests.\n- [x] Two worktrees sharing one store via symlink produce identical `sidecar(\"enrich-drain.lock\")` paths; checked by the new symlink test.\n- [x] All five pinning test files pass with no assertion edits; checked by `pytest` on those files and `git diff --stat`.\n- [x] The two out-of-scope git-dir parsers above are left untouched; checked by `git diff --stat` showing no change to `gitutil.py` or `lock.py`.","env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_store/paths.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/hlc.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/push_state.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_store/sync.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/compact_trigger.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/doctor_locks.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/enrich_drain.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"src/rebar/llm/overlap/queue.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"},{"path":"tests/unit/store/test_store_paths.py","reason":"consolidation edit or new shared module/test"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","managed_refs":[["parent","2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a"],["relates_to","681f-747d-eddc-48ae"],["relates_to","6dd1-c469-5508-4fea"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"2ddd-b523-06da-4b4a","parent_status_uuid":"8c36e5fa-acb5-4aa3-98b3-b410b98dd4e3","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":2,"repos":[],"reverts":[],"status":"closed","tags":["consolidation","janitor","fortnight-review"],"ticket_id":"6f18-05de-beaf-42be","ticket_type":"story","title":"One StorePaths derivation for the canonical store, git dir and sidecars","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["5ef98241-5169-46ac-b9c9-fbff899339f0","ca8cbdc9-ff10-43f0-8bdf-a26aff381eb6","99547fc3-d1e6-4dfa-9da2-1ad6d256ad52","5eab8bde-dc68-4d63-90a8-7a9f1ea7bdf5","5b899ed0-6473-46bd-a4b8-5e491c089b8b","77f17505-20b0-4585-9cf0-86f04d323179","d4d0dae2-0508-45d0-8441-fe215d3bd874","26e1d605-5bde-4dd3-a139-100c364e1780","c3fbb65c-6134-4fe8-ad42-268e43b49dcd","8c36e5fa-acb5-4aa3-98b3-b410b98dd4e3","7cb1347e-312f-400b-a5a5-35d753a52fc4"]},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1787370962866108001,"uuid":"90abbdb8-1ef8-4c09-9d47-13ae4c4e54a8"}